### =====================================================================
###  Instituto Académico — API endpoints (REST Client)
###  Base: http://localhost:3000  |  Las rutas viven bajo /api
###
###  CÓMO USARLO:
###  1) Instalá la extensión "REST Client" (Huachao Mao) en VS Code.
###  2) Levantá MariaDB, aplicá migraciones (npm run prisma:migrate) y
###     creá el admin (npm run create:admin).
###  3) Corré el backend desde /backend con:  npm run dev
###  4) Ejecutá en orden: LOGIN → SELECT ROLE → el resto.
###     Los tokens se capturan automáticamente en {{authToken}}.
###
###  FLUJO DE AUTH (devuelve 2 tokens):
###   POST /auth/login        → devuelve token SIN rol (para /me, /select-role)
###   POST /auth/select-role  → devuelve token CON rol (para el resto)
###
###  ⚠️ Credenciales de ejemplo: reemplazá por las del admin que creaste.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### =====================================================================
### 1. AUTH
### =====================================================================

# @name login
### 1.1 Login (identifier = email o DNI)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "identifier": "admin@instituto.edu.ar",
  "password": "Password1!"
}

### Capturar token sin rol (para select-role / me / logout)
@loginToken = {{login.response.body.$.data.token}}

# @name selectRole
### 1.2 Seleccionar rol → devuelve token CON rol
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-role
Authorization: Bearer {{loginToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "ADMINISTRATIVO"
}

### Token con rol (usado por todas las rutas protegidas)
@authToken = {{selectRole.response.body.$.data.token}}

### 1.3 Obtener perfil del usuario logueado
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 1.4 Registrar usuario (solo ADMINISTRATIVO)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "apellidoNombre": "Ana García",
  "dni": "30123456",
  "email": "ana.garcia@instituto.edu.ar",
  "fechaNacimiento": "1998-05-12",
  "telefono": "1155551234",
  "password": "Password1!",
  "cuil": "20301234567",
  "rol": "ALUMNO",
  "contactoEmergencia": "1112345678",
  "foto": ""
}

### 1.5 Cambiar contraseña (logueado)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "Password1!",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword2!"
}

### 1.6 Olvidé mi contraseña (envía token por email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana.garcia@instituto.edu.ar"
}

### 1.7 Resetear contraseña (con el token del email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "TOKEN_DEL_EMAIL",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword2!"
}

### 1.8 Verificar token de reset (GET)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-reset-token/TOKEN_DEL_EMAIL

### 1.9 Cerrar sesión (logueado)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 1.10 Renovar token con refresh token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "TU_REFRESH_TOKEN"
}

### =====================================================================
### 2. USUARIOS (todas requieren ADMINISTRATIVO salvo /:id permite self)
### =====================================================================

### 2.1 Listar usuarios (paginado + filtros)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?page=1&limit=10&rol=ALUMNO&activo=true&search=
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2.2 Obtener usuario por ID (self o admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2.3 Actualizar usuario (self o admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "telefono": "1155559999",
  "activo": true
}

### 2.4 Cambiar rol de un usuario (admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1/role
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rol": "PROFESOR"
}

### 2.5 Activar/desactivar usuario (admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 2.6 Eliminar usuario (admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

